  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "環境生態與資源永續",
    "sub_ename": "ENVIRONMENTAL ECOLOGY AND RESOURCE SUSTAINABILITY",
    "describe_ch": "由永續發展的概念出發，展示現今世界對於永續發展的想像、作為與挑戰。一方面由環境保育的立場，展示仍在持續中的環保與經濟相互限制的現況，並展示以生物多樣性為主導的「里山倡議」和以溯源解決問題的「自然一步」等模式的永續發展作為。另一方面則由環境正義的立場，展示仍在持續中的經濟與社會相限制的現況，並展示以資源循環利用的「商業生態學」，以綠色服務為導向的「綠領經濟」等模式的永續發展作為。本課程除了展示現有的作為與挑戰，更強調在背景知識的理解，由環境面向要維持的「生物多樣性」，由探討發展模式的「環境經濟學」、「環境社會學」以及因應氣候變遷挑戰的「全球化與在地化」、「氣候變遷政治」等標題概念，以使學員體認自身所處的家園生活的生態發展永續之重要性。",
    "describe_eh": "This course begins with the concept of sustainable development, aiming to cultivate students' understanding and skills through the study of environmental education and environmental justice. Students will develop competencies in communication, observation, collaborative teamwork, discussion, case study analysis, and practical application.\r\nThroughout the course, the instructor will guide students to explore methods of environmental education, understand the principles of environmental justice, and examine current social issues related to these topics. The course places particular emphasis on building foundational knowledge by investigating subjects such as environmental economics, environmental sociology, and climate change politics, among others. This approach helps students recognize the significance of ecological sustainability.\r\nBy the end of the semester, students will acquire basic skills in observation and practical application. It is hoped that they can utilize these methods and experiences to enhance their future endeavors and contribute to a more sustainable world.\r\n",
